posts.text:
Watched Putin's speech at SPIEF this afternoon and it's very frustrating, the man looks increasingly detached from reality. He mentions everything besides the SMO which is barely covered although is the most important thing (its outcome will shape the future of Europe and Russia), his speech is mostly focused on BRICS (which is increasingly divided so it does not look like a safe bet), the importance of developing a national AI based infrastructure, the future of automation and robotic as pillars of Russian economy, the EU is almost in recession (no shit Sherlock...) and Russia's GDP growth is higher than that of the EU and so on...
Ok SPIEF is an economic forum so was not expecting a 100% focus on the SMO but this kind of speech sounds like appeasement of Russian business class who doesn't even want to think about the SMO and believes it was a mistake as their assets in rotten West were frozen and they can't even enjoy some time in Cote d'Azur. 

@eurasianchoice
